//region Setup

// To define a variable, use @var
// Since this variable is not inside a branch, it is treated as global
// You can also use @const for values that will not change
// It's type is inferred as String
@var speaker = "Bittorn"

// To use an external variable, use @export_var
// You can also use @export_const
// Every external variable requires a default value
// This is to ensure no runtime errors occur if the variable isn't set
@export_var player = "Player"

//endregion

=== INTRODUCTION

// Variables declared inside branches are treated as local variables
// This variable's type is inferred as Number
@var age = 21

Hello there!
Welcome to Flow, a simple code-first dialog system.

    + How does it work?
    + Could you repeat that?
        Gotcha.
        => INTRODUCTION
    + What does code-first mean?
        => CODE-FIRST
    + {player is speaker} Hey, I'm $speaker too!
        [Really? What a coincidence!|You've already said that.]
	Are you also $age years old?
	    - Yes!
		Cool!
	    - No.
		A shame.
	> => INTRODUCTION
    + I'm already familiar
        Great! Guess I'll take my leave then.
        => END

> Let's continue.

